              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 2s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Before the new run of words: what did mātraṁ mean, and what did ennāl mean?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 1,
          "type": "input",
          "title": "You'll want to know: അപേക്ഷ",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "അപേക്ഷ (apēkṣa) — \"a request\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Sanskrit apekṣā, made of a piece meaning toward and a root meaning to look. A request is a looking-toward: the eyes go to the person who can grant it before the words do."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "It carries the ക്ഷ pair you have now met twice, in kṣamikkaṇaṁ and in kṣīṇaṁ, this time sitting in the middle of the word rather than at its head."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Beside dayavāyi, which softens whatever follows it, അപേക്ഷ (apēkṣa) names the asking itself and can stand on its own at the head of a written petition."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The first of five words for asking well."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "guided-production",
          "title": "Guided Practice",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 1,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 1s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "apēkṣa",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *apēkṣa*]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "it once more, slowly",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: it once more, slowly]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "prompt",
              "action": "SAY",
              "instruction": "dayavāyi, then apēkṣa, and say which of the two is the asking itself",
              "spoken": true,
              "scored": false,
              "responseSeconds": 8,
              "source": "[YOU SAY: *dayavāyi*, then *apēkṣa*, and say which of the two is the asking itself]"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "type": "recall",
          "title": "Wrap-up Recall",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "pause",
              "seconds": 3,
              "perItem": false,
              "source": "[PAUSE 3s]"
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "What does അപേക്ഷ (apēkṣa) mean? (\"a request\".) Say it once more."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
